Phasmid: screen and window geometry

What:     screen.width/height/avail*, colorDepth, pixelDepth,
          devicePixelRatio, isExtended, orientation, the resolution and
          device-width media queries, and window.outerWidth/outerHeight/
          screenX/screenY come from the profile. The first window opens at
          the profile's size, the headless screen is the profile's display,
          and the browser runs at the profile's device pixel ratio.
Why:      Stock headless reports an 800x600 screen and a 780x580 window, and
          a headful run reports the host's monitor and window manager.
Profile:  display.width, display.height, display.avail_left,
          display.avail_top, display.avail_width, display.avail_height,
          display.color_depth, display.device_pixel_ratio,
          display.is_extended, display.orientation.type,
          display.orientation.angle, window.outer_width, window.outer_height,
          window.screen_x, window.screen_y
Hooks:    content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_view_base.cc
          GetNewScreenInfosForUpdate;
          content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_impl.cc
          SendScreenRects, GetVisualProperties;
          chrome/browser/ui/window_sizer/window_sizer.cc
          DetermineWindowBoundsAndShowState;
          chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.cc BasicStartupComplete;
          chrome/app/BUILD.gn
Contexts: main, iframe; workers have no screen. isExtended is false in
          cross-origin iframes (permissions policy), as in stock.
Guard:    tests/guards/display/screen-window.py

